# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Weights & Biases -------------------------------------------------------
# Live W&B run payloads are large and machine-written. Provenance lives in
# runs/<experiment_id>/resolved_config.json (which records wandb_run_id), so
# nothing scientific is lost by not tracking these.
wandb/
code/wandb/
!archive/**/wandb_runs_*/

# --- Per-run output directories (plan.md 2.2) -------------------------------
# runs/<experiment_id>/ IS the canonical record, so the small provenance and
# metric files ARE tracked (updated_rules.md 9: every figure must be traceable
# to exact run IDs). Only the large or regenerable payloads are excluded.
runs/**/checkpoint.pt
runs/**/*.pt
runs/**/stdout.log

# --- Model checkpoints outside the archive ----------------------------------
# The two checkpoints under archive/pre_finalization/ are tracked as evidence of
# the pre-audit state and are unaffected by this rule.
#
# T11.5: the exception is scoped to `pre_finalization` deliberately. It used to
# read `!archive/**/*.pt`, which was correct when those two files were the only
# archived checkpoints -- but `archive/t9_1_undeclared_group_runs/` and
# `archive/t10_smoke_1epoch/` later added 11 more, ~155 MB, and the blanket
# exception would have committed all of them. Those runs are INVALIDATED; the
# evidence a future reader needs is their `config.json`,
# `resolved_config.json`, `metrics.json`, `results.tsv` and
# `INVALIDATED.md` -- all still tracked. A checkpoint of an invalidated run is
# not citable and is regenerable from its own recorded config, so it is weight,
# not evidence. The files remain on disk; only tracking is declined.
*.pt
!archive/pre_finalization/**/*.pt

# --- Global output filenames that Phase 0 abolished -------------------------
# Listed so a stray legacy write is never committed by accident.
/best_model.pt
/results.tsv
/final_run_metrics.json
/sweep_results.csv
/1block_results.csv
/2block_results.csv
code/best_model.pt
code/results.tsv
code/final_run_metrics.json

# --- Gate smoke runs (T-L0.3b) ----------------------------------------------
# Gate 5 LAUNCHES two real 1-epoch training runs so that its provenance and
# metric-contract checks grade a directory produced by the code under test rather
# than whichever archived run sorted last by mtime. That is deliberate and is what
# fixed T-L0.3b -- but it means every execution of the suite deposits a fresh
# `__rN` directory, and the suite is expected to run after every commit (T-LX.0).
#
# These are regenerable gate artifacts, not evidence: nothing cites them, they are
# 1-epoch proxies that may never enter a table, and the next suite run recreates
# them. Tracking them would grow the repository without bound in exchange for
# nothing citable. This is NOT a deletion (CLAUDE.md 6) -- the directories stay on
# disk; only tracking is declined, exactly as for invalidated checkpoints above.
#
# `runs/t_l03_mor_timing_seed44__fa9339bc` is deliberately NOT covered: the
# changelog cites it as the run on which the eleven-key `"N/A"` metric contract was
# verified at HEAD, so it is evidence and is tracked.
runs/t67_provenance_check*/
runs/t67d_provenance_check*/

# --- Language corpora (T-L2.2) ----------------------------------------------
# `data/lang/<corpus>/` is BUILT, not authored: `data/lang/build_language_dataset.py`
# reproduces it from a pinned HF dataset revision recorded in the manifest. So the
# split here is between the files that DEFINE the dataset and the files that ARE it.
#
# TRACKED (the definition, ~550 KB per corpus):
#   dataset_meta.json  -- hf_dataset/hf_config/hf_revision, generator_commit,
#                         raw_lines, raw_bytes, unk_literal_occurrences, vocab_size,
#                         seq_len, splits, token_counts, dropped_tail_tokens,
#                         per-split sha256, dataset_version. Every number any
#                         language result is conditioned on is in this file, and
#                         `code/test_language_data.py` grades the .npy files against
#                         the hashes it records -- so a fresh clone can VERIFY a
#                         rebuild rather than merely repeat it.
#   tokenizer.json     -- the fitted BPE. Deliberately tracked even though it is
#                         regenerable: BPE merge order depends on the `tokenizers`
#                         version's tie-breaking, so a rebuilt tokenizer is not
#                         guaranteed byte-identical, and a different tokenizer makes
#                         every recorded loss number incomparable. This is the one
#                         build artifact that is cheaper to store than to trust.
#   token_family.npy   -- 8 KB (int8 x 8192): the frozen oracle POS partition every
#                         routing-agreement, Hungarian, AMI and purity number is
#                         measured against (T-L3.1). Tracked for the tokenizer's
#                         reason and then some -- rebuilding it costs ~15 min of
#                         tagging plus a specific nltk model version, and a
#                         different partition silently redefines what
#                         `routing_agreement_with_pos` means.
#
# NOT TRACKED (the payload):
#   *.npy        -- 6.6 MB for wikitext-2, ~260 MB for wikitext-103. Fully determined
#                   by tokenizer.json + the pinned revision + seq_len, and hash-checked
#                   against the manifest on every test run. `token_decile.npy` and
#                   `token_family_shuffled.npy` are covered by this rule and NOT by the
#                   exception above, deliberately: the first is a 2-second bincount over
#                   train.npy, the second a seeded permutation of token_family.npy, so
#                   both reproduce exactly from a fixed seed and no external model.
#                   `token_family.npy` does not -- it needs a specific nltk model --
#                   which is the whole basis of the distinction.
#   *_text.txt   -- the materialized train text (10.9 MB / 539 MB). An intermediate
#                   consumed only by the tokenizer trainer.
#   *.bin        -- the raw uint16 stream `pack_split` writes before reshaping. Removed
#                   on success; listed so a crashed build's leftover is never committed.
#   _hf_cache/   -- 537 MB of `datasets` Arrow shards. HF's cache, not our artifact: it
#                   sits under `data/lang/` only because the builder passes `cache_dir`
#                   there to keep a 539 MB download off the `C:` system drive (T-L0.2).
#                   The pinned `hf_revision` in each manifest is what makes the fetch
#                   reproducible, so the cache carries nothing the manifest does not.
#                   It staged itself on the first `git add data/lang/` -- hence the rule.
#
# As everywhere else in this file, this declines TRACKING, not existence -- the files
# stay on disk (CLAUDE.md 6).
data/lang/**/*.npy
!data/lang/**/token_family.npy
data/lang/**/*_text.txt
data/lang/**/*.bin
data/lang/_hf_cache/

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
